    "body": "> First of all, you need to install a Python on iOS. Then you need to build pyTorch and other dependencies for it. In fact, the separation can be really slow, so I haven't tried it, though it seems possible to achieve. \r\n\r\nPython on iOS? I am using LibTorch (c++ version of pyTorch). I am now rewriting all of the layers in C++ (HDemucs, Demucs,Encoders/Decoder), so will see how far I get. Why not use JITed model? I want to debug it step by step on par with python code, to see if ther are any discrepancies. Was mainly checking if someone else did it and can see issues with my approach. ",
